Compensation Terms
Our comprehensive executive compensation program includes the following elements of compensation:
Base salary - refers to the annual fixed (non-variable) pay rate;
Cash incentive - refers to our Executive Incentive Compensation Plan (“EICP”), which is our annual short-term cash incentive plan and includes quarterly cash incentive payments;
Total cash compensation - refers to base salary plus cash incentive payments;
Equity-Based awards - include restricted stock units (“RSUs”), cash-settled units ("CSUs") and stock options, all of which use time-based vesting, and performance-based shares which are awarded contingent on meeting the specified performance objectives and, if achieved, include time-based vesting with respect to the share award; and
Total direct compensation - refers to total cash compensation and equity awards.
